      "text": "Consciousness is a subjective experience where the individual feels aware of themselves, encompassing self-awareness and the ability to reflect on thoughts and actions. It arises from complex brain processes, particularly involving the prefrontal cortex, which facilitates decision-making and self-reflection. The hard problem of consciousness seeks to understand why subjective experiences exist, despite our grasp of brain mechanisms. While we know parts of the brain involved in self-awareness, the underlying neural mechanisms for consciousness remain elusive.",
